<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35854" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕtulcus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		peto; cf. petulans <i>init.</i>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>butting</i>, <i>apt to butt</i>, with the horns or head (<b>poet.</b> and post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 368</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haedi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caper velaries,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					7, 3, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>frisky</i>, <i>wanton</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haedi petulci dicti ab appetendo: unde et
					meretrices petulcas vocamus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. G. 4, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
